    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0248" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg180"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Sir F.
                        Bruce</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 6, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir:</hi> I have not yet received the
                    transcripts of the records of the late capital trials which have taken place in
                    Canada. It can well be conceived that the papers are voluminous, and the delay
                    is, therefore, unavoidable; nevertheless the 13th of December is near at hand. I
                    beg leave, therefore, to ask if you have it in your power to inform me of the
                    probable disposition of those cases.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear sir, very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frederick W. A. Bruce</hi>, &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
